  "title": "Abduction and murder of Giacomo Matteotti",
  "summary": "On 10 June 1924 the Socialist deputy Giacomo Matteotti was seized by five men on Lungotevere Arnaldo da Brescia in Rome while walking to Montecitorio, forced into a car and probably killed inside it. He had denounced the Fascist Party in the Chamber eleven days earlier; his body was found on 16 August in the Quartarella wood at Riano.",
